        "notes": "Served as taco bowls for toddlers over rice without tortillas for easier eating"
      },
      "prep_time": "20 minutes",
      "cook_time": "25 minutes",
      "ingredients": [
        "2 lbs tilapia fillets (7-8 oz per adult serving)",
        "2 ripe peaches, finely diced",
        "1 cup cherry tomatoes, finely diced",
        "1/2 cup fresh corn kernels",
        "3 cups dry white rice (yields approximately 6 cups cooked)",
        "8 small corn tortillas (for adults; serve toddlers as a rice bowl)",
        "Juice of 2 limes",
        "1 tbsp olive oil",
        "2 tbsp fresh cilantro, chopped",
        "Salt to taste"
      ],
      "steps": [
        "Cook white rice according to package directions. When done, stir in lime juice from 1 lime and 1 tbsp chopped cilantro. Set aside.",
        "Make peach salsa: combine diced peaches, diced cherry tomatoes, corn kernels, remaining lime juice, and remaining cilantro. Season with salt. Set aside.",
        "Pat tilapia dry and season lightly with salt.",
        "Heat 1 tbsp olive oil in a nonstick skillet over medium-high heat. Cook tilapia 3-4 minutes per side until fish flakes easily and is cooked through. Flake into large pieces.",
        "Warm corn tortillas in a dry skillet or microwave.",
        "For adults: serve 2 corn tortillas filled with flaked tilapia and topped with peach salsa alongside 1.5 cups cilantro lime rice.",
        "For toddlers: serve flaked tilapia as a taco bowl over 3/4 cup cilantro lime rice with a spoonful of peach salsa on the side."
      ],
      "kids_tasks": [
        "Toddlers can help stir the peach salsa ingredients together in a bowl with a spoon.",
        "Older toddler can help squeeze lime juice with a hand juicer."
      ]
    },
